== How to opt in ==

Add <code>class=lead-hero</code> to the File link:

 <nowiki>[[File:Kicksecure-Desktop.png|thumb|class=lead-hero|A full-bleed hero lead image.]]</nowiki>

The image is emitted first, above the title, matching how feature articles open. Use it sparingly, only when the lead image is strong enough to lead the whole page.

== Accessibility note ==

Because the hero comes before the title, a screen reader meets the image and its caption before the page name. That is an informed, opt-in trade for the striking opening, and matches how the newspapers that use this shape are built. For ordinary documentation pages prefer treatment A or B, which keep the title first on screen as well as in the markup.

